        "id": 1176029
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-06T13:40:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I considered this question and the live variable here made me to write this codes. The reason is that since live indicates the real id from chip, it can be still legal if it is one of supported sources.\n\nFor example, what if board_get_product_id can be called after tcpci_tcpm_init then the judgement of expected product_id can be came from chip itself in run time and in the factory / RMA flow we can catch this result in SSFC for example. Finally we don\u0027t need any additional source of truth?\n\nI am still experiencing this plan.",
      "parentUuid": "e2ad56de_63f74d31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 316,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 336,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "7a9fcffc0a1f5732ea5df959d763bc5853a1a77d",
